cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenPerfusion in research, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenPerfusion: open-source CT perfusion processing for acute stroke"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-02
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OpenPerfusion/OpenPerfusion"
url: "https://github.com/OpenPerfusion/OpenPerfusion"
authors:
  - family-names: Scott
    given-names: Will
    affiliation: "Division of Neurology, University Health Network, University of Toronto"
keywords:
  - CT perfusion
  - acute ischemic stroke
  - deconvolution
  - Tmax
  - ischemic core
  - RAPID
  - ISLES 2018
abstract: >-
  An open-source, delay-insensitive CT perfusion pipeline (block-circulant SVD /
  oSVD / Fourier-Wiener deconvolution, automatic AIF/VOF selection, rCBF < 30 %
  core and Tmax > 6 s hypoperfusion volumes, mismatch and DEFUSE-3 target
  profile) validated against RAPID output on the 94 ISLES 2018 training scans.
  Research use only; not a medical device.
